<Base title="NFTs | The Crypto Realm" description="NFTs are more than pictures: royalties for creators, true ownership for gamers, perks from brands and proof of ownership for real-world assets.">
  <section class="container page-title">
    <div class="eyebrow">NFTS</div>
    <h1>NFTs Are More Than Pictures</h1>
    <p class="subtle">An NFT is a digital certificate of ownership recorded on a blockchain. Whoever holds it can prove it’s theirs, trade it without asking anyone’s permission, and, depending on how it’s built, unlock perks and even earn from it.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container section" id="uses">
    <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">WHAT NFTS CAN DO</div><h2>Ownership for everybody</h2></div></div>
    <div class="use-grid">
      <div class="card use"><span>✦</span><h3>Artists, photographers &amp; creators</h3><p>Sell your work straight to your audience, with no gallery or platform deciding for you. You can set a royalty so you earn a cut every time your work is resold, on the marketplaces that honor it.</p></div>
      <div class="card use"><span>⚔</span><h3>Gamers</h3><p>In blockchain games that support it, your skins, weapons and items live in your own wallet. They’re yours to keep, trade or sell on an open marketplace, instead of being locked inside one company’s game. Imagine owning every asset you earn.</p></div>
      <div class="card use"><span>◈</span><h3>Brands &amp; loyalty</h3><p>Companies can issue collectible NFTs that work like a loyalty card. Hold the collectible and unlock deals, early access or members-only perks. And because it’s in your wallet, it’s yours to keep, trade or sell.</p></div>
      <div class="card use"><span>⌂</span><h3>Real-world ownership</h3><p>NFTs can also represent a claim on real things like tickets, memberships, property or vehicles, recorded on a blockchain. This area is still early, and the legal side varies by country, but the idea is ownership you can prove.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="note">This is just the beginning. Anything that can be owned can be represented on a blockchain, and that puts the power back with creators and owners.</p>
  </section>

